  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "She is first named on the Jia caravan treehouse when Gu Yue Yao Ji calls her granddaughter Yao Le after the girl snaps at a clerk over a lost Liquor worm bid.",
      "chapters": [
        111
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_yao_ji",
        "gu_liquor_worm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the same caravan visit, the day before her Awakening Ceremony, she presses Yao Ji for that Liquor worm as a promised gift.",
      "chapters": [
        110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Crowd talk soon gives the full clan form Gu Yue Yao Le and places her in the coming Awakening Ceremony, with Yao Ji bidding ahead to pave her way.",
      "chapters": [
        113
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "That early stretch sits on Qing Mao Mountain inside the Gu Yue clan.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "fac_gu_yue_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is a young girl with black hair, a peach-like small mouth, eyes shining like crystals, and a slightly chubby face.",
      "chapters": [
        147
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She is beautiful.",
      "chapters": [
        148
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "She is fifteen years old, with a frail body and slim legs. She has a cute appearance, black lustrous eyes, a round nose slightly pointing up, skin blushing like peach blossoms, and two rows of white clean teeth.",
      "chapters": [
        151
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Qing Shu later names her Yao Ji’s granddaughter, a new student that year with B grade aptitude, and explains Yao Ji’s failed treehouse bid for a Liquor worm meant for her.",
      "chapters": [
        123
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "granddaughter-of-the-medicine-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_qing_shu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng also urges Fang Yuan to sell, calling sister Yao Le a good person who would care for the worm.",
      "chapters": [
        124
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "granddaughter-of-the-medicine-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yao Ji does obtain a Liquor worm from the caravan afterward and gives that worm to Yao Le.",
      "chapters": [
        147
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "granddaughter-of-the-medicine-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the wolf tide she runs a healing station as a young rank one Gu Master. Xiong Jiao Man greets her by name, praises her medical skill and Yao Ji’s benevolent line, and places her among Qing Mao Mountain’s top ten rising stars. Yao Le then asks her grandmother to punish Fang Yuan for extorting Xiong Jiao Man, and clansmen credit her persuasion when the medicine hall orders holders of Nine Leaf Vitality Grass to hand the Gu over for unified leaf production.",
      "chapters": [
        147
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "granddaughter-of-the-medicine-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "char_xiong_jiao_man",
        "gu_nine_leaf_vitality_grass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yao Ji’s staff later reports her near the east door leading the healing team and refusing to stay at the rear. Yao Ji treats that front-line work as political capital for the day Yao Le inherits the medicine hall.",
      "chapters": [
        149
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "granddaughter-of-the-medicine-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When a frenzy lightning wolf breaks the eastern gate, Yao Ji races out because Yao Le is still there. Xiong Jiao Man tries to pull Yao Le clear, but Soundwave Gu force flings Yao Le past the broken gate into the wolf packs outside the village. Fang Yuan guides her out of the immediate encirclement with spoken directions and moonblades, then reveals himself in a remote forest and knocks her out.",
      "chapters": [
        150
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "eastern-gate-and-capture",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan carries her into a mountain cave, ties her to a rock, and takes every Gu on her body. The text states she is about fifteen. He brings a black bear under Bear Enslavement Gu; the bear kills her with a paw strike that breaks her neck, then eats her while Fang Yuan watches.",
      "chapters": [
        151
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_bear_enslavement_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He forces the bear to finish the remains and refines Man-beast Life Burial Gu, a rank three expenditure Gu whose tattoo shows Yao Le’s face, then uses that Gu to break through to rank three. The recipe for that Gu requires a virgin girl who is a Gu Master of at least C grade aptitude, with A or B grade improving the chance of success.",
      "chapters": [
        152
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_man_beast_burial_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For three days Yao Ji searches and refuses to accept the loss. Witnesses last saw Yao Le fleeing wolf encirclement, and the medicine hall treats her as missing without a corpse.",
      "chapters": [
        152
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yao Ji still names her the medicine faction’s inheritor while she is missing.",
      "chapters": [
        153
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the elder hall Fang Yuan calls the B grade granddaughter dead; Yao Ji denies it, and Fang Yuan then attacks her search parties as a waste of healing Gu Masters. Narration after Yao Ji faints treats Yao Le’s death and Yao Ji’s downfall as the medicine faction’s decline.",
      "chapters": [
        154
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later states that his third Liquor worm on Qing Mao Mountain came from Yao Le’s body, and that he destroyed that worm so the Tie father and daughter could not investigate her case.",
      "chapters": [
        212
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "liquor-worm-recollection",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes the name as Gu Yue Yao Le, with Yao Le and Miss Yao Le as the short forms used around her.",
      "chapters": [
        111
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "No Chinese characters for her personal name appear in the English chapter text used here. The Awakening Ceremony itself is not printed with her grade on the page; Qing Shu’s later B grade line is the direct aptitude statement after she is already a student.",
      "chapters": [
        113
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan takes every Gu from her body in the cave, but the only Gu from that haul later named is the Liquor worm; no vital Gu or other healing Gu set is named for her.",
      "chapters": [
        151
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_vital_gu",
        "sys_healing_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
